  "description": "Talk about body parts, express symptoms, and navigate visits to the doctor or pharmacy.",
  "guidebook": "### Talking About Symptoms\n\nTo say that a body part hurts, attach the subject particle **-이/가** to the body part followed by **아파요** (hurts/is sick):\n* **머리가 아파요.** (My head hurts / I have a headache.)\n* **배가 아파요.** (My stomach hurts.)\n\n### Taking Medicine in Korean\nIn English, we say \"take medicine,\" but in Korean, you literally *eat* medicine using the verb **먹다**:\n* **약을 먹어요.** (I take medicine.)\n\n### Catching a Cold\nTo express that you have caught an illness like a cold, use the idiom **감기에 걸리다**:\n* **감기에 걸렸어요.** (I caught a cold.)\n\nWhen resting, Koreans often say **푹 쉬세요** (Please rest well).",
